**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Scope:** this exported KB and its triage guidance.
**Replaces:** [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), preserved as accepted history.
This record does not claim the course's live desk or production software has been changed.

## Context

The [review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review) shows distinct mechanisms behind matching
subjects. Browser-derived intake labels also disagree with tenant-specific classification.
A merge can conceal a different defect and leave it without an engineering ticket.

## Decision

Deduplicate by supported cause, not subject equality. Join the tenant directory and compare
channel, form version and locale using the supplied `causeOf`/`sameCause` functions. Read
report bodies before merging to retain contradictory or unexplained evidence. Keep one
engineering issue per established cause, with counts based on distinct report IDs.

## Consequences

- Same subject with different causes stays in separate tickets.
- Different subjects with the same supported mechanism can share a ticket.
- Unknown tenants and unexplained symptoms need review; “no cause” is not a matching cause.
- New reports or tenant changes require recomputing counts and rebuilding the KB.
- This needs more desk attention than subject-only matching, but avoids hiding a second fix.

